<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Prayer times, tall — the second picker entry for the same widget.

  Not a second widget. `PrayerWidgetLargeProvider` is `PrayerWidgetProvider`
  with a different name, and `selectLayout` has always chosen the card from
  the measured size rather than from the provider class, so an instance
  placed from here is the same card the other entry places, two rows tall
  from the start.

  Two entries because Android's picker shows ONE preview per provider, at the
  size `targetCell*` names. This widget means something different at one row
  and at two — at one it is the six times and what is next; at two the city,
  the Hijri date and the full list come with it — and a single entry has to
  pick one of those to show and be wrong about the other. A person scrolling
  the picker should be able to see the version they want.

  TWO ROWS, not three. Three was the default because three rows is ~321dp
  at 420dpi, past the 265dp where the practice graph appears, and the graph
  was the thing this entry was for. But a launcher row is not a fixed dp:
  two rows is ~210dp on that 420dpi grid and ~294dp on a 1080x2400 phone,
  which is past 265dp — so on the grid most people have, two rows already
  brings the graph, and it costs a third of a home screen less. Where it
  does not, the card is one drag from it, and the layout has always been
  chosen from the measured size, so nothing else has to change.

  This file replaces the retirement. The entry used to be
  `widget_description_large_retired` on `widgetCategory="keyguard"`, which is
  a category the home-screen picker does not list — so the provider existed,
  rendered correctly, and had no way in. Retiring it made sense when it drew
  a genuinely different and worse layout; it draws the current one now.
-->
<!-- TWO ROWS IN THE PICKER, NOT ONE — issue #31.

     `targetCellWidth`/`targetCellHeight` are API 31 and say 4x2, and on a
     launcher that honours them this entry previews at twice the height of
     the short one. Not every launcher does. EMUI falls back to
     minWidth/minHeight, and both providers advertised 250x60 — so the
     picker showed two 4x1 tiles with almost the same label, which is
     exactly what was reported: "duplicate widgets (4x1) in the choices".

     `minHeight` is the size the picker PLACES it at; `minResizeHeight` is
     how small it may then be dragged. Separating the two is what this
     entry always meant: place it tall, shrink it if you want the strip.
-->
<!--
  The API 31+ copy: identical to ../xml/prayer_widget_tall_info.xml, but hidden from the picker.
  The Glance card of the same name is the entry now; this provider stays
  registered only so widgets a user placed before the switch keep drawing
  (docs/rewrite-plan.md, 4.3). Delete with the provider, once nobody has one placed.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:configure="com.prayer_times.PrayerWidgetConfigureActivity"
    android:description="@string/widget_description_tall"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/prayer_widget_strip"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="130dp"
    android:previewImage="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/prayer_widget_tall_preview"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable|hide_from_picker"
    android:minResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="60dp"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:maxResizeWidth="500dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="600dp" />
